# Dance Maniax (G*874 VER. JAA), Konami 2000: a game, from what dmx-install left (its NVRAM). Power-on: the RTC is
# initialised and the game set up from the flash (no NOTE to answer), the loading screens, attract
# by frame ~8000. Two coins at frame 9000, then Start every 300 frames through the caution, MODE
# SELECT (MILD), HOW TO PLAY and the music select (their defaults: BROKEN MY HEART); the first
# stage, with its MP3 music, played by breaking all four of player 1's hand sensors (both beams of
# the lower ones) every 8 frames from frame 10900: a full combo, CLEARED by ~16800, the result,
# then the second stage's music select. Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60
# frames, to compare HIRAKU's 573 core with MAME through a song.
game dmx

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 9000 press "Coin 1" 8
at 9040 press "Coin 1" 8
at 9300 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 9600 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 9900 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 10200 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 10500 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 10800 press "1 Player Start" 8
from 10900 every 8 press "P1 D-Sensor U L" 4
from 10902 every 8 press "P1 D-Sensor U R" 4
from 10904 every 8 press "P1 D-Sensor D0 L" 4
from 10904 every 8 press "P1 D-Sensor D1 L" 4
from 10906 every 8 press "P1 D-Sensor D0 R" 4
from 10906 every 8 press "P1 D-Sensor D1 R" 4
from 0 every 60 snap
at 17700 quit
